Ladybird renders each list-box option with its own computed style.
Blink assigns the option in ListBoxSelectType::ManuallyAssignSlots(),
and WebKit reads its color in RenderListBox::paintItemForeground().
Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0 and WebKit 26.5 all painted the
author colors when the option belonged to a group.

Ladybird skips options without layout boxes when finding the next row.
Gecko checks for an option frame in IsOptionInteractivelySelectable().
Chrome and Firefox skipped a hidden option and a hidden group, then
reached the group option after its stylesheet made it visible. WebKit
selected the hidden option in the same keyboard test.

Shift+End selects the enabled options between the anchor and the last
visible row, including CSS-hidden options. Firefox and WebKit included
them in the same range. Chrome selected only the visible options.
